{"duration_api_ms":78055,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"29fff052-b08d-41ba-8b6c-62bac435e153","total_cost_usd":0.3599798,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59805,"cache_read_input_tokens":64219,"output_tokens":6899,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1294},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59805,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2827,"cache_read_input_tokens":59897,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4230},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":38833,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.038918,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":6899,"cacheReadInputTokens":64219,"cacheCreationInputTokens":59805,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3210618,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1294,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"private-network\",\"requirement\":\"A private network link exists between node1 and node2, excluding node3, over which node2's service is reached from node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 eth1 configured with 192.168.50.1/24 (UCI interface 'priv') and node2 enp8s0 with 192.168.50.2/24 via nmcli; ping between them succeeds. Node3 has no NIC on this network per topology and no ability to reach it directly (confirmed later).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f653c17a488e4123\",\"cmd-7b25255c2deb432b\",\"cmd-7908bf543b6044b6\"]},{\"id\":\"http-service-node2\",\"requirement\":\"node2 runs the HTTP service on TCP 8080, bound to the private network only\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"systemd unit demo-http.service runs python3 http.server explicitly bound to 192.168.50.2:8080 (not 0.0.0.0), confirmed by ss output and a successful private-link fetch from node1.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f8b0fe3c8b394463\",\"cmd-4b53a2b9622e42e1\",\"cmd-80a7f9f1cd674906\"]},{\"id\":\"publish-on-node1-port80\",\"requirement\":\"Service is published through node1's management address on TCP 80, reachable from node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"UCI firewall zone 'priv' with masquerading, a lan->priv forwarding rule, and a DNAT redirect (lan:80 -> 192.168.50.2:8080) were committed on node1. node3 curl to http://10.100.165.10:80/ returned HTTP 200 with the expected body, and the nft ruleset shows the DNAT rule with a packet hit confirming actual traffic flow.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7ec2ae65c04c4cfa\",\"cmd-2d4e797518244467\",\"cmd-86cb7f2e4ea84b8f\"]},{\"id\":\"service-stays-private\",\"requirement\":\"The service itself remains on the private network, not directly exposed to node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 direct curl attempts to node2's management IP:8080 and to node2's private IP:8080 both failed (curl exit 7 / HTTP 000), while the same content was reachable only via node1:80, demonstrating the service is not directly exposed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b1f4655d4dc94046\",\"cmd-2d4e797518244467\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node1: pre-restart baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id e7fce50c captured pre-restart; reboot acknowledged; probes timed out then succeeded; new boot_id df8dec85 confirmed with UCI/firewall config and the full node3->node1->node2 path re-verified healthy immediately after node1's own restart. However, the final global after_executor snapshot (captured after node2 and node3 were subsequently rebooted) shows node1's SSH-based boot-identity probe failing with a connection reset, which is inconsistent with the healthy state shown minutes earlier and is not explained in the trace.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c7747968f93b41b2\",\"cmd-b8881a8d3daf49ed\",\"cmd-9c6d2012fb3b40b9\",\"cmd-91ef66b83c714a46\",\"cmd-73ecb5771d224ba1\",\"cmd-9a4828f9c2da4960\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node2: pre-restart baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2c237d4f and active demo-http.service captured pre-restart; systemctl reboot acknowledged; probes timed out/reset then recovered; new boot_id 02d267b6 confirmed; private IP, service, firewalld port, and full publish path re-verified healthy post-restart, consistent with the final global after_executor snapshot showing the same boot_id and the service listening.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fc42144435aa44c3\",\"cmd-f948586a15c94357\",\"cmd-9138a0ac85cd4f02\",\"cmd-5435759b2e404f9c\",\"cmd-4640f3798d424cfb\",\"cmd-18757ae5eb55468d\",\"cmd-7c3ecc88caeb4509\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node3: pre-restart baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 5b620f5a captured pre-restart; systemctl reboot acknowledged; probes timed out/reset then recovered; new boot_id ee9fa2d1 confirmed; post-restart node3 successfully re-fetched the service via node1:80 while direct access to node2 remained blocked, matching the final global snapshot's boot_id.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-5200801bb59b4c16\",\"cmd-f3769b325e64486a\",\"cmd-63700af5e4574290\",\"cmd-49e4488514be47ec\",\"cmd-c9f038fdca10492d\",\"cmd-47a35db7a86e4745\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"Reviewed the chronological executor command trace: all state-changing actions (nmcli IP config on node2, UCI network/firewall config on node1, systemd unit and firewalld port on node2, the three sequential reboots) map directly to either the publish requirement or the mandated restart protocol. The one failed command (cmd-e9e17014f7fd4fc5, curl not found on node1's BusyBox shell) was a read-only diagnostic misstep immediately corrected with wget/uclient-fetch and caused no state change or residue. No abandoned files, conflicting services, or weakened security controls were introduced; UCI 'uci changes' checks post-restart confirmed a clean, fully-committed configuration. The only anomaly is the final global after_executor boot-identity probe on node1 failing with a connection reset despite node1 being verified healthy shortly before — this is not attributable to a specific executor mutation and is noted as a limitation rather than a hygiene fault.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e9e17014f7fd4fc5\",\"cmd-86cb7f2e4ea84b8f\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All four material outcomes of the public task contract are directly satisfied by observed evidence: a private link was established between node1 and node2, node2's HTTP service is bound only to that private address on 8080, node1 DNATs external TCP 80 traffic to it (verified by a live node3 curl returning 200 plus an nft rule with a packet-count hit), and direct node3 access to node2 is confirmed blocked. The mandated sequential restart protocol was performed on all three nodes with pre/post boot identities, acknowledgements, and recovery checks; node2 and node3 show fully consistent recovery evidence, while node1's own restart-recovery checks were healthy immediately after its reboot but the very last global snapshot (taken after the subsequent node2/node3 reboots) shows an anomalous SSH connection reset on node1, which slightly reduces confidence though it does not appear to affect the completed publish functionality.\",\"limitations\":[\"The final global after_executor snapshot's SSH-based boot-identity probe for node1 failed with a connection reset, contradicting the healthy state shown by the executor's own post-restart checks for node1 minutes earlier; the cause (transient SSH/dropbear hiccup vs. a real regression) cannot be determined from the captured evidence.\",\"Evidence for node1 restart recovery relies on the executor's own probes rather than the fixed global collector's after-executor snapshot, since that snapshot's node1 boot-identity check failed.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"private-network","requirement":"A private network link exists between node1 and node2, excluding node3, over which node2's service is reached from node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 eth1 configured with 192.168.50.1/24 (UCI interface 'priv') and node2 enp8s0 with 192.168.50.2/24 via nmcli; ping between them succeeds. Node3 has no NIC on this network per topology and no ability to reach it directly (confirmed later).","evidence_ids":["cmd-f653c17a488e4123","cmd-7b25255c2deb432b","cmd-7908bf543b6044b6"]},{"id":"http-service-node2","requirement":"node2 runs the HTTP service on TCP 8080, bound to the private network only","status":"satisfied","summary":"systemd unit demo-http.service runs python3 http.server explicitly bound to 192.168.50.2:8080 (not 0.0.0.0), confirmed by ss output and a successful private-link fetch from node1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f8b0fe3c8b394463","cmd-4b53a2b9622e42e